SDAutoLogin on Debian and Ubuntu
================================

What the package installs
-------------------------
  /usr/bin/SDAutoLogin                         the program, built without a tray
  /usr/lib/systemd/system/sdautologin.service  the service that runs it
  /usr/lib/sysusers.d/sdautologin.conf         the user it runs as

Giving it an account
--------------------
  sudo -u sdautologin SDAutoLogin --home=/var/lib/sdautologin \
       --username=s1234567 --password=SECRET --isp=@zgyd --save config --show
  sudo systemctl restart sdautologin

Leave the service suffix out for the campus network itself. For the settings
page, add --settings=127.0.0.1:8088 to the ExecStart line of the unit
("systemctl edit sdautologin") and open the address the log prints
("journalctl -u sdautologin"): it carries a one-time token.

Settings and log
----------------
  /var/lib/sdautologin/config.json      the settings, the password only when it
                                        was asked to keep it
  /var/lib/sdautologin/logs/app.log     the log, rotated when it passes 4 MiB

Both stay where they are when the package is removed or purged.
